  "final_text": "**Don't send 279.7 MWh yet. It's only 11 months of data, because the September 2025 invoice is missing.**\n\nWhat I checked in `electricity_2025.csv`:\n\n- **The duplicate was handled correctly.** October (EL-25-10, 38,700 kWh) appears twice, once as the e-invoice and once as a scan with the same number and amount. Counting it once is right.\n- **September 2025 isn't there at all.** The months go straight from 2025-08 to 2025-10, with no invoice EL-25-09.\n- **The office manager's figure matches the 11 months.** Jan–Aug plus Oct–Dec comes to 279,700 kWh = **279.7 MWh**. The note calls this the \"full year\", but it isn't.\n\nThe missing month matters. According to the company profile, tank cooling peaks in September and October. August was 32.1 MWh and October 38.7 MWh, so September was probably one of the highest months of the year, likely around 30–40 MWh. The real annual total is probably about **310–320 MWh**, so 279.7 would understate it by roughly 10%. That's an estimate, though, and I wouldn't send it to the bank.\n\n**What to do:**\n1. Get the September 2025 invoice (EL-25-09) from Lumivolt Snabduvanje or from accounting. It's October 2026 now, so it was issued long ago. If it's not in the books, it may also never have been booked or paid, which is worth checking.\n2. Enter **279.7 MWh + September's kWh ÷ 1,000**.\n3. If the bank needs a number before you have the invoice, label it clearly as an estimate (\"11 months metered, September estimated\"). This loan is for PV sized against your consumption, so the bank may compare your figure with the grid operator's data.\n\nThe note was marked \"draft, not checked\", and this is the gap it missed.",
